{"duration_api_ms":9904,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"3a665ec2-4e67-45d1-b97b-3ca7acd75c70","total_cost_usd":0.0629836,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4419,"cache_read_input_tokens":60638,"output_tokens":774,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":44},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4419,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":6,"outputTokens":774,"cacheReadInputTokens":60638,"cacheCreationInputTokens":4419,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0629836,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":44,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":4,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've implemented `to_cents` in `src/money.py`, and both tests in `python3 -m unittest tests.test_money` pass.\n\nIt uses `Decimal` with `ROUND_HALF_UP` instead of Python's built-in `round()`, which rounds halves to the nearest even number. The amount is converted with `Decimal(str(amount))` rather than `Decimal(amount)`. A float like `1.005` is actually stored as `1.00499999…`, so passing it to `Decimal` directly would round down to 100. Going through `str()` uses the number as it's written, so `to_cents(1.005)` gives `101` as the test expects.\n\nThe hint from an earlier run (use `Decimal` and `ROUND_HALF_UP`) matched what the code needed. I didn't rely on it as proof: the test results are what confirm the fix.","ttft_ms":2282,"type":"result","duration_ms":10026,"uuid":"5b4a7173-31ae-4b26-8b97-d9168ac7b6e0","ttft_stream_ms":1829,"time_to_request_ms":38,"first_content_frame_ms":1829,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
